### Background and motivation

StackTrace already contains a constructor that accepts a single frame, accepting multiple frames would seem a logical continuation and allows for nice resolution of stack frames captured from an existing StackTrace object. 

Because `ToString(TraceFormat traceFormat, StringBuilder sb)` uses `_numOfFrames` rather than the virtual `FrameCount` when calling `GetFrame(int)`, it's unreliable (minus setting the field via reflection) to call `ToString()` on a class derived from `StackTrace` that would allow the specification of a specific set of frames (rather than one frame).

### API Proposal

```csharp
namespace System.Diagnostics;

public partial class StackTrace
{
    //Additional constructor
    public StackTrace(StackFrame[] frames)
    {
        _stackFrames = frames;
        _numOfFrames = frames.Length;
    }
}
```


### API Usage

```csharp
// Get a real stack trace
var realTrace = new StackTrace(true)
// Filter out frames that aren't of interest (things that could identify a customer, generated code, etc.)
var filteredFrames = FilterToDesiredFrames(realTrace.GetFrames());
// Construct a fake trace containing the desired frames
var fakeTrace = new StackTrace(filteredFrames);

// Using the prettification StackTrace applies to its frames
Console.WriteLine(fakeTrace);
```


